# Repo-root .dockerignore
#
# This file controls what is sent to the Docker daemon as build context for any
# build run from the repo root — which is every build here, because apps/web is
# an npm workspace and its Dockerfile must be able to see the ROOT
# package.json + package-lock.json (see apps/web/Dockerfile).
#
# Two reasons to keep this tight:
#   1. Speed. The build context is tarred and uploaded to the daemon on every
#      build; node_modules and .venv alone are hundreds of megabytes.
#   2. SECURITY. The .env rules below are NOT an optimisation. Anything left in
#      the build context can end up in an image layer, and image layers are
#      readable by anyone who can pull the image — `docker history` and
#      `docker save` both expose them, and deleting the file in a later layer
#      does NOT remove it from the earlier one. A leaked .env inside a published
#      image is a real credential-disclosure incident, not a tidiness problem.
#      Secrets are injected at RUN time (compose `environment:`, Railway/Vercel
#      variables), never baked in at BUILD time.

# --- Dependencies (reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile) ----------
node_modules
**/node_modules
.npm
.pnpm-store

# --- Build output (rebuilt inside the image; a host .next is the wrong arch) -
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
dist
build
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Python service artefacts ----------------------------------------------
.venv
**/.venv
venv
**/venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# --- SECURITY: never ship environment files (see header) --------------------
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

# --- VCS / CI / editor ------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# --- Tests, reports, logs ---------------------------------------------------
test-results
**/test-results
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
**/*.log

# --- Docs and prose (not needed at runtime) ---------------------------------
docs
**/docs
*.md
!apps/web/app/**/*.md

# --- Deploy configs for other targets ---------------------------------------
.vercel
vercel.json
docker-compose.yml

# Launch/marketing assets: GIF cuts, render sources and the outreach list.
# None of it is part of any runtime image — it added 21 MB to a 76 MB build
# context — and launch/social/src/nul is a Windows reserved-device-name
# artifact that Docker cannot extract at all: `COPY . .` dies with
# "Error processing tar file(exit status 1): operation not permitted",
# which names no file and so is near-impossible to trace back. Excluded here
# as well as in .gitignore, because .gitignore has no effect on the Docker
# build context.
launch
